From c80b0f64afe35e0ef4bb7fdff13a05ab3d5b7020 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 22:15:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Why It Went This Way gives the techniques apart from the
 language, and the guide names the language where it explains fit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The review of the first cut found the settled role's line "your techniques are N% of the way" printing fitOf's
`demands`, which the language had joined: a fluent speaker whose techniques were all mastered read 93%, and the line
never named the language the fit had weighed. Fit now also carries `techniques`, the techniques alone, and the line
says the language in a sentence of its own, naming the weaker of the actor's two languages, the one the fit counts
(`languageFitWords`). `demands` and `fit` are untouched, so casting's chance, an agent's reach and every figure the
first cut measured stand as they were; splitting the language out of `demands` instead would have moved them all.

The guide and the tutorial said less than the code: Auditions gave the fit as genres and techniques, Finding Work's
eligibility, needs and refusals left the language out, and the tutorial's résumé had no languages. They name it now.
The Languages entry's fit read showed the fit's figures ("80% as well"), and the card said "Casting reads", both of
which STYLE.md keeps from the player; they say it in words, from `suitsWords`, which reads LANGUAGE_FIT, so a figure
changed changes the words with it.

Comments the first cut had made untrue were brought up to date: the projobs header and slateReach's fit bullet, fitOf's
own doc, PartPrep's three stacked doc comments (merged into one), and content/slate.ts, which now says why the language
draw went in under SLATE_VERSION 1 rather than a new version: a save's own copy of a posted part is the one the session
keeps.

Left to integration, since the record is the primary's: tests/b20-guide-wiring.test.ts fails until
docs/verification/audit-2026-10-21/areas/guide/wiring.json is rewritten for the new Work On Your … control and the
moved handler lines (`node tools/wiring.mjs --write`, then that line's reading).

